# ── A dependency-VERSION trap worth remembering ─────────────────────────────
# `packages/contracts` declares zod "^3.24.1", but that range resolves to 3.25.x,
# and the two disagree about `z.string().datetime()`: 3.24.1 requires seconds
# (HH:MM:SS), 3.25.x makes them optional. Transcribing the regex from the
# DECLARED version made the Kotlin port reject `2026-07-25T10:00Z` — an instant
# the platform accepts and its own merge suite exercises on purpose. When porting
# a validator, check the version that actually RESOLVES, not the one in the
# manifest. (Fixed in VaultContracts.kt; see the KDoc on DATETIME_REGEX.)

